# Build context for both application images (`backend/Dockerfile`, `frontend/Dockerfile`).
#
# The backend image needs the project definition, the lockfile and the source; the
# frontend image needs `frontend/`. Everything else is excluded, and two exclusions are load-bearing:
#
#   * `.env` — a deployment's credentials reach the container through `env_file` at run time. Baking
#     them into an image would put real API keys in every layer, every registry copy and every
#     `docker save`.
#   * `.venv`, `node_modules`, `datasets`, `dist` — the working tree, not the artifact. Sending them
#     would make the context gigabytes wide and the build minutes long.

.git
.gitattributes
.gitignore
.github
.venv
.ruff_cache
.pytest_cache
.pyright
.probe
.pi
.impeccable
.agents
datasets
dist
docs
evals
node_modules
**/node_modules
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
